{"assets":["/statement-assets/92e173e82baf40a5b8e27cb87b575f37c28cfd036d3babe0bd60dfa64b824837.png","/statement-assets/131ce51661be5c5f9cf3f74207b778d6a63705798519f07e8bd16b673040ab74.png"],"contentKind":"statement","contestId":"1012","diagnostics":[],"document":{"children":[{"attrs":{"level":1,"role":"title"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"C. Hills"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"time_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"time limit per test"},{"kind":"text","text":":"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"1 second"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"memory_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"memory limit per test"},{"kind":"text","text":":"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"512 megabytes"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"body"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Welcome to Innopolis city. Throughout the whole year, Innopolis citizens suffer from everlasting city construction. "}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"From the window in your room, you see the sequence of "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"n"},{"kind":"text","text":" hills, where "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"i"},{"kind":"text","text":"-th of them has height "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"ai"},{"kind":"text","text":". The Innopolis administration wants to build some houses on the hills. However, for the sake of city appearance, a house can be only built on the hill, which is strictly higher than neighbouring hills (if they are present). For example, if the sequence of heights is "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"5, 4, 6, 2"},{"kind":"text","text":", then houses could be built on hills with heights "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"5"},{"kind":"text","text":" and "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"6"},{"kind":"text","text":" only."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The Innopolis administration has an excavator, that can decrease the height of an arbitrary hill by one in one hour. The excavator can only work on one hill at a time. It is allowed to decrease hills up to zero height, or even to negative values. Increasing height of any hill is impossible. The city administration wants to build "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"k"},{"kind":"text","text":" houses, so there must be at least "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"k"},{"kind":"text","text":" hills that satisfy the condition above. What is the minimum time required to adjust the hills to achieve the administration's plan?"}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"However, the exact value of "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"k"},{"kind":"text","text":" is not yet determined, so could you please calculate answers for all "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"k"},{"kind":"text","text":" in range "},{"attrs":{"alt":"","src":"/statement-assets/92e173e82baf40a5b8e27cb87b575f37c28cfd036d3babe0bd60dfa64b824837.png"},"kind":"image"},{"kind":"text","text":"? Here "},{"attrs":{"alt":"","src":"/statement-assets/131ce51661be5c5f9cf3f74207b778d6a63705798519f07e8bd16b673040ab74.png"},"kind":"image"},{"kind":"text","text":" denotes "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"n"},{"kind":"text","text":" divided by two, rounded up."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"input_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The first line of input contains the only integer "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"n"},{"kind":"text","text":" ("},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"1 ≤ n ≤ 5000"},{"kind":"text","text":")—the number of the hills in the sequence."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Second line contains "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"n"},{"kind":"text","text":" integers "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"ai"},{"kind":"text","text":" ("},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"1 ≤ ai ≤ 100 000"},{"kind":"text","text":")—the heights of the hills in the sequence."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"output_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Print exactly "},{"attrs":{"alt":"","src":"/statement-assets/131ce51661be5c5f9cf3f74207b778d6a63705798519f07e8bd16b673040ab74.png"},"kind":"image"},{"kind":"text","text":" numbers separated by spaces. The "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"i"},{"kind":"text","text":"-th printed number should be equal to the minimum number of hours required to level hills so it becomes possible to build "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"i"},{"kind":"text","text":" houses."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"samples"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Examples"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"children":[{"attrs":{"role":"sample_input"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"5\n1 1 1 1 1\n"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample_output"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"1 2 2 \n"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"children":[{"attrs":{"role":"sample_input"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"3\n1 2 3\n"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample_output"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"0 2 \n"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"children":[{"attrs":{"role":"sample_input"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"5\n1 2 3 2 2\n"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample_output"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"0 1 3 \n"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"note"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Note"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"In the first example, to get at least one hill suitable for construction, one can decrease the second hill by one in one hour, then the sequence of heights becomes "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"1, 0, 1, 1, 1"},{"kind":"text","text":" and the first hill becomes suitable for construction."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"In the first example, to get at least two or at least three suitable hills, one can decrease the second and the fourth hills, then the sequence of heights becomes "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"1, 0, 1, 0, 1"},{"kind":"text","text":", and hills "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"1, 3, 5"},{"kind":"text","text":" become suitable for construction."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"document"},"index":"C","problemCode":"1012C","schema":2,"sourceKind":"html","sourceUrl":"https://codeforces.com/contest/1012/problem/C"}